# Add a resource

1. Generate it, with its fields (`name:type`, types `string`, `text`,
   `email`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `date`; add `:optional` or
   `:unique`):

   ```sh
   go tool anetos make:crud Article title:string body:text published:bool
   ```

   It writes the model (`app/models/`), its migration, the handlers
   (`app/handlers/<table>.go`, with the input struct and its `validate`
   tags), [[if .API]]the routes under `/api/v1` (`routes/<table>.go`, added to
   `routes/api.go`), a test, and updates `openapi.json`[[else]]the pages ([[if .Inertia]]`frontend/src/pages/<Models>/`: `Index`, `Show`
   and `Form`, built from `src/components/ui[[.Ext]]`'s components[[else]]`views/<table>.templ`[[if .HasUI]], built from `views/ui`'s
   components[[end]][[end]]), the routes (`routes/<table>.go`, added to `routes/web.go`),
   a link in the layout's nav, the pages' text (`locales/en/<table>.yaml`)
   and a test[[end]].
2. `go run . migrate`
3. Adjust what it wrote: validation rules in the input struct's
   `validate` tags (`required|max:200`), [[if .API]]the response struct, the
   list's filters and sorts[[else]]the form's fields, the list's columns[[end]], queries with the typed columns
   (`models.ArticleCols.Title`). After changing a model: `go tool anetos generate`.
4. To limit it to logged-in users, register its routes in a group with
   the login check (after `make:auth`; see `go tool anetos docs [[if .API]]api-accounts[[else]]accounts[[end]]`).
5. `go tool anetos check`

It refuses when a file or the migration exists: pick another name, or
write the parts by hand. Docs: `go tool anetos docs crud`,
`go tool anetos docs guides/models`, `go tool anetos docs guides/queries`,
`go tool anetos docs guides/validation`.
